1
00:00:07,293 --> 00:00:11,971
(This program contains indirect advertisements.)

2
00:00:12,438 --> 00:00:13,778
Where are we going?

3
00:00:14,348 --> 00:00:15,608
What if we're going abroad?

4
00:00:16,278 --> 00:00:17,978
This is totally insane.

5
00:00:17,978 --> 00:00:19,078
(What will be the mission location for Round 4?)

6
00:00:20,848 --> 00:00:22,088
I didn't know we could get out from here.

7
00:00:24,158 --> 00:00:25,518
Where are we going?

8
00:00:26,088 --> 00:00:29,058
Where will we compete? It made me imagine all kinds of possibilities.

9
00:00:30,698 --> 00:00:32,928
We're at Incheon Airport at night.

10
00:00:33,768 --> 00:00:34,868
We're going up.

11
00:00:37,098 --> 00:00:39,668
I felt stunned, like I got hit on the head.

12
00:00:40,638 --> 00:00:43,008
(Where are they headed?)

13
00:00:45,478 --> 00:00:46,478
Over here?

14
00:00:51,648 --> 00:00:52,718
This is incredible.

15
00:00:53,688 --> 00:00:55,118
What could the next mission be?

16
00:00:55,318 --> 00:00:59,288
I will now announce the mission for Round Four.

17
00:00:59,358 --> 00:01:00,388
Already?

18
00:01:00,928 --> 00:01:02,888
- Here comes the mission.
- All of a sudden?

19
00:01:02,888 --> 00:01:04,228
The Round Four mission is called...

20
00:01:09,028 --> 00:01:10,738
Morning at the Airport.

21
00:01:10,968 --> 00:01:11,968
Are we making breakfast?

22
00:01:12,368 --> 00:01:13,438
Are we making breakfast?

23
00:01:14,238 --> 00:01:16,138
- What a surprise.
- "Morning at the Airport?"

24
00:01:16,268 --> 00:01:18,108
- Morning?
- Morning at the airport is...

25
00:01:18,108 --> 00:01:19,538
the busiest time of day...

26
00:01:19,538 --> 00:01:22,108
with the most flights and the highest number of passengers.

27
00:01:23,878 --> 00:01:26,048
(The final gateway to the final round)

28
00:01:26,648 --> 00:01:28,448
(Morning at the Airport)

29
00:01:28,548 --> 00:01:30,788
(The start of a journey to destinations around the world)

30
00:01:30,818 --> 00:01:32,888
(Of different nationalities)

31
00:01:32,888 --> 00:01:34,328
(With different purposes)

32
00:01:34,328 --> 00:01:35,888
(Countless people)

33
00:01:36,488 --> 00:01:38,598
(A special moment before departure)

34
00:01:38,828 --> 00:01:43,398
(Where travelers can enjoy performances on their way out)

35
00:01:44,138 --> 00:01:46,138
(Incheon International Airport's departure area)

36
00:01:46,598 --> 00:01:49,068
(The departure terminal is today's business district.)

37
00:01:49,338 --> 00:01:51,608
(The airport food court that connects tourists with K-food)

38
00:01:51,608 --> 00:01:54,208
Each team will open a station in the food court...

39
00:01:54,478 --> 00:01:57,148
and serve breakfast...

40
00:01:57,148 --> 00:01:59,078
from 6am to 9am.

41
00:01:59,578 --> 00:02:02,318
- I didn't imagine this.
- In the morning?

42
00:02:03,418 --> 00:02:07,088
I was wondering what approach we should take.

43
00:02:07,228 --> 00:02:10,958
Will there be more foreign or Korean customers?

44
00:02:10,958 --> 00:02:11,958
(Who will be the main customers? Koreans or foreigners?)

45
00:02:11,958 --> 00:02:15,268
Something you can eat easily in the morning.

46
00:02:15,268 --> 00:02:18,038
The key is food that people can eat quickly before leaving.

47
00:02:18,038 --> 00:02:19,638
It's a place where people can get this and that.

48
00:02:19,638 --> 00:02:21,768
They can share different dishes.

49
00:02:21,768 --> 00:02:23,608
Since they're about to leave Korea,

50
00:02:23,608 --> 00:02:24,838
it must be something distinctively Korean.

51
00:02:24,838 --> 00:02:25,838
(Is Korean food advantageous in this district?)

52
00:02:25,838 --> 00:02:29,178
This round will be conducted as a blind competition.

53
00:02:29,178 --> 00:02:30,208
(Round 4 will be a blind competition.)

54
00:02:30,448 --> 00:02:31,878
That's a relief. It works in our favor.

55
00:02:32,548 --> 00:02:34,318
For this mission,

56
00:02:34,318 --> 00:02:37,888
you can add one more part-time employee to your team.

57
00:02:37,888 --> 00:02:38,888
We can add an employee.

58
00:02:39,158 --> 00:02:41,228
The ingredient budget is up to each team.

59
00:02:41,628 --> 00:02:43,958
The cost will be deducted from the final sales.

60
00:02:44,098 --> 00:02:46,758
The menu and pricing are entirely up to the team.

61
00:02:47,028 --> 00:02:48,028
- Net profit?
- Net profit?

62
00:02:48,028 --> 00:02:49,198
We're competing based on net profit?

63
00:02:50,168 --> 00:02:51,638
In this mission,

64
00:02:51,638 --> 00:02:53,708
only the top three teams...

65
00:02:54,108 --> 00:02:57,108
with the highest sales will survive.

66
00:02:57,778 --> 00:02:58,838
This will be hard.

67
00:03:00,408 --> 00:03:01,408
Three teams?

68
00:03:01,908 --> 00:03:03,408
Let's survive this round as well.

69
00:03:03,408 --> 00:03:05,878
- Whatever it takes, let's make it.
- Let's make it.

70
00:03:06,018 --> 00:03:08,048
We just have to win. I'm confident.

71
00:03:08,748 --> 00:03:12,318
In this mission, there will be a special rule.

72
00:03:12,318 --> 00:03:13,358
Another rule?

73
00:03:14,888 --> 00:03:15,888
There will be...

74
00:03:17,328 --> 00:03:18,858
a bidding war.

75
00:03:18,858 --> 00:03:20,258
(Bidding war)

76
00:03:20,528 --> 00:03:21,728
- What?
- "Bidding?"

77
00:03:22,428 --> 00:03:23,738
Is it because of the shop location?

78
00:03:24,598 --> 00:03:26,368
- It's a battle of locations.
- Bidding for shop locations?

79
00:03:26,468 --> 00:03:27,768
Does each location cost a different amount?

80
00:03:28,368 --> 00:03:29,408
What does it mean?

81
00:03:32,738 --> 00:03:33,848
It must be him.

82
00:03:34,608 --> 00:03:38,448
Hello, I'm auctioneer Kwak Jong Woo. I'll be overseeing the bidding war.

83
00:03:41,618 --> 00:03:42,618
It's an auction.

84
00:03:42,918 --> 00:03:44,318
Right in front of you,

85
00:03:44,318 --> 00:03:47,828
there is a total of seven shop properties up for auction.

86
00:03:48,788 --> 00:03:49,988
(Street Restaurant Fighter)

87
00:03:54,128 --> 00:03:55,168
The lights turned on.

88
00:04:01,608 --> 00:04:04,538
(7 food courts)

89
00:04:06,208 --> 00:04:08,648
(A. Korean food station 1)

90
00:04:09,808 --> 00:04:12,548
(B. Korean food station 2)

91
00:04:13,648 --> 00:04:16,188
(C. Thai food station)

92
00:04:17,018 --> 00:04:19,158
(D. Hot dog station)

93
00:04:19,418 --> 00:04:21,528
(E. Pork cutlet station)

94
00:04:21,758 --> 00:04:24,098
(F. Chinese food station)

95
00:04:24,528 --> 00:04:27,128
(When you walk deeper inside)

96
00:04:27,898 --> 00:04:30,838
If you win a shop through the auction,

97
00:04:31,238 --> 00:04:34,038
including the kitchen equipment, appliances, and tableware,

98
00:04:34,038 --> 00:04:35,808
you will have to use everything exactly as is.

99
00:04:35,808 --> 00:04:37,138
(The existing kitchen and equipment must be used.)

100
00:04:37,408 --> 00:04:39,538
Also, there's a total of five sales hooks...

101
00:04:40,138 --> 00:04:42,448
to help promote your shop.

102
00:04:42,448 --> 00:04:43,848
(Sales hook 2: A set of 3 medium LED posters)

103
00:04:43,848 --> 00:04:46,378
(Sales hook 3: A set of 3 banners)

104
00:04:46,418 --> 00:04:49,248
(Sales hooks 4, 5: Upper and lower display cases)

105
00:04:49,248 --> 00:04:50,858
Everything you receive...

106
00:04:51,258 --> 00:04:53,218
has to be obtained through the auction.

107
00:04:53,218 --> 00:04:54,328
(Shops and sales hooks can only be acquired through bidding.)

108
00:04:54,328 --> 00:04:56,258
Any money spent during the auction...

109
00:04:56,258 --> 00:04:57,828
will be deducted from your sales.

110
00:04:58,598 --> 00:05:02,568
(The more you spend, the bigger the loss.)

111
00:05:02,828 --> 00:05:05,038
Since these are actual restaurants,

112
00:05:05,038 --> 00:05:06,368
all the interiors are different.

113
00:05:07,168 --> 00:05:09,338
We have to use the equipment that's already inside.

114
00:05:09,968 --> 00:05:11,538
Looking at the kitchens,

115
00:05:11,938 --> 00:05:14,108
- not a single one is the same.
- I know.

116
00:05:14,478 --> 00:05:17,718
We're probably in for a chaotic battle.

117
00:05:17,918 --> 00:05:21,648
(The bidding war starts.)

118
00:05:21,918 --> 00:05:23,518
We're about to start...

119
00:05:23,518 --> 00:05:24,788
- the shop auction.
- The shop?

120
00:05:25,258 --> 00:05:26,888
The opening bid is ten dollars.

121
00:05:27,358 --> 00:05:29,088
Every time someone raises their paddle,

122
00:05:29,328 --> 00:05:31,498
the bid goes up by ten dollars.

123
00:05:32,328 --> 00:05:33,428
I'm curious.

124
00:05:33,828 --> 00:05:35,668
I feel like everyone is thinking the same thing.

125
00:05:36,168 --> 00:05:38,868
First, Station A is a Korean food station.

126
00:05:39,498 --> 00:05:42,008
(Station A used to sell bibimbap and soup with rice.)

127
00:05:42,508 --> 00:05:44,008
It has two regular burners,

128
00:05:44,508 --> 00:05:45,908
two low burners,

129
00:05:46,478 --> 00:05:49,148
and one rotating stir-fry wok.

130
00:05:50,408 --> 00:05:53,518
(A classic kitchen for Korean cuisine)

131
00:05:53,518 --> 00:05:56,148
You can even make fried rice in here, right?

132
00:05:56,148 --> 00:05:57,988
- Four burners?
- We can make other things too.

133
00:05:57,988 --> 00:05:59,388
- Spicy stir-fried pork?
- This is the best.

134
00:06:00,058 --> 00:06:01,588
We wanted Station A.

135
00:06:01,858 --> 00:06:03,158
We can make bibimbap.

136
00:06:03,158 --> 00:06:04,358
- Right.
- We can make so many things.

137
00:06:04,358 --> 00:06:06,128
I really liked the kitchen.

138
00:06:06,258 --> 00:06:07,298
If I were a customer,

139
00:06:08,168 --> 00:06:09,828
I'd only get either A or B.

140
00:06:09,828 --> 00:06:11,968
(Korean food A, Korean food B)

141
00:06:12,268 --> 00:06:14,308
asked the staff who work here.

142
00:06:14,768 --> 00:06:15,868
It has to be Korean food.

143
00:06:16,338 --> 00:06:17,408
They said that there are a lot of foreigners here.

144
00:06:17,638 --> 00:06:18,878
- We should sell Korean food.
- Right.

145
00:06:19,108 --> 00:06:20,338
What sells the best here?

146
00:06:20,748 --> 00:06:21,908
I'd say Korean food.

147
00:06:21,978 --> 00:06:23,008
Korean food?

148
00:06:23,108 --> 00:06:24,678
For breakfast, we must sell Korean food.

149
00:06:24,678 --> 00:06:25,878
Yes, but...

150
00:06:26,048 --> 00:06:29,118
(Most of them prefer the Korean food stations.)

151
00:06:29,448 --> 00:06:30,658
Jong In, let's join them.

152
00:06:30,658 --> 00:06:32,358
I want to hear what everyone else is saying.

153
00:06:34,728 --> 00:06:36,728
(Quietly)

154
00:06:37,528 --> 00:06:39,198
(Peeking)

155
00:06:39,228 --> 00:06:40,258
Naengmyeon?

156
00:06:40,498 --> 00:06:42,168
What is it? Please tell us.

157
00:06:42,268 --> 00:06:44,798
Both Sung Hoon's team and Sang Hyun's team want...

158
00:06:45,068 --> 00:06:47,098
the same thing as us.

159
00:06:47,668 --> 00:06:49,538
- A is the best location.
- Yes.

160
00:06:50,438 --> 00:06:51,978
The competition will be brutal.

161
00:06:52,138 --> 00:06:54,408
- Seriously.
- How much will we have to spend?

162
00:06:54,408 --> 00:06:55,408
(Many teams are hoping to win Korean food station A.)

163
00:06:55,508 --> 00:06:57,918
It will be a game of reading the room.

164
00:06:57,918 --> 00:06:58,978
I'm definitely taking this one.

165
00:06:59,818 --> 00:07:01,418
The bidding starts at ten dollars.

166
00:07:01,748 --> 00:07:02,948
Every bid goes up by ten dollars.

167
00:07:02,948 --> 00:07:04,658
- We're winning this one.
- The auction will begin.

168
00:07:05,358 --> 00:07:06,358
Ten dollars.

169
00:07:06,718 --> 00:07:07,988
It's a ten-dollar bid.

170
00:07:08,158 --> 00:07:10,088
(Kim Hoon, 10 dollars)

171
00:07:10,428 --> 00:07:11,458
Twenty dollars.

172
00:07:11,458 --> 00:07:12,698
We have a 30-dollar bid.

173
00:07:13,058 --> 00:07:14,428
Forty dollars? I'll ask again.

174
00:07:14,668 --> 00:07:16,198
Choi Sang Hyun was a little faster.

175
00:07:16,198 --> 00:07:17,438
Fifty dollars is still available.

176
00:07:17,898 --> 00:07:19,238
We have a 50-dollar bid.

177
00:07:19,238 --> 00:07:20,538
Sixty dollars is available.

178
00:07:22,268 --> 00:07:23,268
- Sixty dollars.
- Shall we go for it?

179
00:07:23,838 --> 00:07:25,278
- Anyone for 60 dollars?
- Come on, 60 dollars is nothing.

180
00:07:25,538 --> 00:07:26,808
Jung Ho Young, 60 dollars.

181
00:07:26,808 --> 00:07:28,678
- Don't try to stir things up.
- How about 70 dollars?

182
00:07:29,508 --> 00:07:31,218
Seventy dollars. Eighty dollars.

183
00:07:31,478 --> 00:07:32,518
Ninety dollars.

184
00:07:33,118 --> 00:07:34,548
Ninety dollars. How about a hundred?

185
00:07:34,548 --> 00:07:35,718
- Take your time.
- I'll ask again.

186
00:07:35,718 --> 00:07:37,918
Anyone for 110 dollars?

187
00:07:38,658 --> 00:07:40,958
- Anyone for 120 dollars?
- Hoon is flexing.

188
00:07:40,958 --> 00:07:42,588
- I'm going all in.
- One hundred and twenty dollars.

189
00:07:42,728 --> 00:07:43,728
One hundred and thirty dollars.

190
00:07:43,728 --> 00:07:45,098
Don't let them see you wavering.

191
00:07:45,558 --> 00:07:48,228
Our strategy was to intimidate them...

192
00:07:48,328 --> 00:07:49,968
so that they drop out.

193
00:07:51,838 --> 00:07:53,098
Let's think about it when we get to Station B.

194
00:07:54,208 --> 00:07:55,608
One hundred and thirty dollars.

195
00:07:55,868 --> 00:07:57,978
For 130 dollars, Jung Ho Young was a bit faster.

196
00:07:58,378 --> 00:07:59,478
One hundred and forty dollars.

197
00:07:59,738 --> 00:08:01,148
I bet they'll go all the way.

198
00:08:02,278 --> 00:08:03,748
One hundred and fifty dollars. One hundred and sixty dollars?

199
00:08:03,908 --> 00:08:06,048
Jung Ho Young, I'll take your 170-dollar bid.

200
00:08:06,248 --> 00:08:08,218
- Gosh.
- One hundred and eighty dollars.

201
00:08:08,218 --> 00:08:09,718
- They'll go all the way.
- How about 190 dollars?

202
00:08:09,718 --> 00:08:11,788
(Jung Ho Young, 190 dollars)

203
00:08:11,918 --> 00:08:13,788
We have a 200-dollar bid.

204
00:08:13,788 --> 00:08:15,588
- Anyone for 210 dollars?
- Look at Hoon.

205
00:08:15,928 --> 00:08:17,228
Two hundred dollars? Goodness.

206
00:08:18,858 --> 00:08:21,698
They might be deliberately driving up the price.

207
00:08:23,368 --> 00:08:25,898
He's definitely going to do it. Let's drive up the price...

208
00:08:26,438 --> 00:08:27,968
to make him spend more money.

209
00:08:28,438 --> 00:08:30,438
Keep going. We'll go up to this price.

210
00:08:31,208 --> 00:08:34,048
We have a bid. Two hundred and twenty dollars is available.

211
00:08:34,048 --> 00:08:37,578
(The auction price is treated as rent and deducted from the sales.)

212
00:08:37,678 --> 00:08:39,918
- Trust me.
- Anyone for 220 dollars?

213
00:08:40,248 --> 00:08:41,448
Two hundred and twenty dollars.

214
00:08:41,448 --> 00:08:42,748
- How about 230 dollars?
- Goodness.

215
00:08:43,088 --> 00:08:45,018
- It's too expensive.
- How about 230 dollars?

216
00:08:45,958 --> 00:08:47,558
- How about 230 dollars?
- I'll buy even if it's 500 dollars.

217
00:08:47,758 --> 00:08:50,088
- Anyone for 230 dollars?
- It's too much.

218
00:08:50,128 --> 00:08:51,528
How is it anyway?

219
00:08:51,528 --> 00:08:52,558
It's the best location.

220
00:08:52,658 --> 00:08:54,698
- That's a strategy too. Raise it.
- Shall I raise it?

221
00:08:54,698 --> 00:08:56,098
(Jung Ho Young, 330 dollars)

222
00:08:56,098 --> 00:08:57,098
He'll do it.

223
00:08:58,068 --> 00:08:59,298
It's 340 dollars.

224
00:08:59,798 --> 00:09:01,838
- We have a 350-dollar bid.
- Will we be okay?

225
00:09:01,838 --> 00:09:04,178
- How about 360 dollars?
- Keep going!

226
00:09:04,178 --> 00:09:06,308
- We have a 360-dollar bid.
- Again?

227
00:09:06,508 --> 00:09:07,578
How about 370 dollars?

228
00:09:07,578 --> 00:09:08,748
(Hoon, 360 dollars)

229
00:09:08,748 --> 00:09:11,178
We have a 370-dollar bid.

230
00:09:11,178 --> 00:09:12,518
How about 380 dollars?

231
00:09:12,648 --> 00:09:13,778
Immediately without hesitation...

232
00:09:13,778 --> 00:09:14,848
That's how it's done.

233
00:09:15,088 --> 00:09:16,148
How about 370 dollars?

234
00:09:16,488 --> 00:09:17,888
Hold on a second.

235
00:09:17,888 --> 00:09:19,188
- Let's think.
- This is...

236
00:09:20,118 --> 00:09:22,528
I knew right then. If I backed down now, I'd lose it.

237
00:09:22,788 --> 00:09:24,358
I tried to look confident with my arms crossed.

238
00:09:25,328 --> 00:09:27,798
We have a 390-dollar bid.

239
00:09:28,068 --> 00:09:29,798
Four hundred...

240
00:09:30,128 --> 00:09:32,898
- Four hundred and ten dollars.
- Goodness.

241
00:09:32,898 --> 00:09:34,168
(Hoon, 400 dollars)

242
00:09:34,208 --> 00:09:36,508
(Will Station A be awarded at this price?)

243
00:09:36,838 --> 00:09:38,708
- Anyone for 410 dollars?
- Even if they win,

244
00:09:39,338 --> 00:09:40,338
they wouldn't make any money.

245
00:09:41,478 --> 00:09:44,618
Four hundred dollars.

246
00:09:45,518 --> 00:09:46,648
Gosh, that's impressive.

247
00:09:46,648 --> 00:09:49,148
Chef Kim Hoon won it with a 400-dollar bid.

248
00:09:49,148 --> 00:09:50,248
- Congratulations.
- Thank you.

249
00:09:50,248 --> 00:09:52,758
Now if we want to win something, we have to bid around 400 dollars.

250
00:09:53,018 --> 00:09:55,058
This could be the lowest price.

251
00:09:55,428 --> 00:09:57,028
It could be the lowest price.

252
00:09:57,328 --> 00:09:58,428
Don't be scared.

253
00:09:58,858 --> 00:10:01,698
I was really happy. With this station,

254
00:10:01,728 --> 00:10:04,698
I'd at least make it to the top three.

255
00:10:05,238 --> 00:10:07,398
The second auction is...

256
00:10:07,808 --> 00:10:09,168
for Station B.

257
00:10:10,108 --> 00:10:12,878
(A place specializing in earthen pot dishes, stews, stir-fried dishes)

258
00:10:13,308 --> 00:10:15,908
(B earthen pot)

259
00:10:16,008 --> 00:10:17,408
As a Korean food station,

260
00:10:17,778 --> 00:10:19,148
it has 2 5-burner cooktops...

261
00:10:20,078 --> 00:10:21,788
and a food warming cabinet.

262
00:10:22,388 --> 00:10:24,688
No other place has a warming cabinet this big.

263
00:10:25,058 --> 00:10:27,318
For rice-based items, it's a really good option.

