00:19:55,328 --> 00:19:56,488
(Kim Hoon: A, minus 400 dollars, Jung Ho Young: B, minus 50 dollars)

527
00:19:56,488 --> 00:19:57,658
(Kim Ho Yoon: C, minus 600 dollars, Lee Sung Hoon: D, minus 400 dollars)

528
00:19:57,658 --> 00:19:58,798
(Hong Seok Cheon: E, minus 450, Choi Sang Hyun: F, minus 400)

529
00:19:58,798 --> 00:19:59,798
(Lee Yeon Bok: G, minus 10 dollars)

530
00:20:00,028 --> 00:20:01,528
This isn't about sales.

531
00:20:02,028 --> 00:20:03,768
- Including the material cost.
- The material cost.

532
00:20:03,868 --> 00:20:05,138
- It's about operating income.
- Operating income.

533
00:20:05,138 --> 00:20:07,198
In the end, it's about how much you make profit.

534
00:20:07,198 --> 00:20:08,268
That's right.

535
00:20:08,338 --> 00:20:10,608
We must think carefully about...

536
00:20:10,608 --> 00:20:11,938
how many servings to prepare.

537
00:20:12,978 --> 00:20:14,238
Let's drink this.

538
00:20:15,778 --> 00:20:17,008
They got sangria too.

539
00:20:20,778 --> 00:20:22,948
It's very fruity and refreshing.

540
00:20:22,948 --> 00:20:24,888
The orange smells so strong. It's so good.

541
00:20:25,488 --> 00:20:26,788
I don't feel too comfortable.

542
00:20:29,728 --> 00:20:32,098
Surprisingly, it goes well with ham and cheese too.

543
00:20:32,258 --> 00:20:33,458
- Does it?
- Yes.

544
00:20:33,798 --> 00:20:35,868
Will we be okay? I'm so worried.

545
00:20:36,428 --> 00:20:38,198
We need to be really clever with our menu.

546
00:20:39,768 --> 00:20:42,068
(2 weeks later)

547
00:20:42,438 --> 00:20:45,338
(7 hours before the business starts)

548
00:20:45,338 --> 00:20:47,378
(Food court)

549
00:20:47,378 --> 00:20:48,648
(Street Arena)

550
00:20:48,648 --> 00:20:50,248
(Chef's Cooking Makes Us Happy, Eat And Flight)

551
00:20:50,248 --> 00:20:51,718
(Itaewon Class Thai)

552
00:20:51,718 --> 00:20:52,978
(Hororok Samgye Soft Tofu)

553
00:20:52,978 --> 00:20:54,888
Street Restaurant Fighter.

554
00:20:55,848 --> 00:20:58,718
Welcome to Round Four.

555
00:20:59,618 --> 00:21:02,358
(The fourth Street Arena, Incheon International Airport)

556
00:21:02,628 --> 00:21:03,728
I won't go home.

557
00:21:04,258 --> 00:21:05,758
I've come this far. I can't go home.

558
00:21:05,758 --> 00:21:06,798
I agree.

559
00:21:06,858 --> 00:21:09,498
The seven teams opening their stores in the airport food court...

560
00:21:09,728 --> 00:21:12,698
have new signboards, and they can choose the menu...

561
00:21:12,698 --> 00:21:14,398
and the price freely.

562
00:21:15,368 --> 00:21:16,668
From the total sales,

563
00:21:17,368 --> 00:21:18,608
station rental,

564
00:21:18,608 --> 00:21:19,878
(Total sales minus station rental)

565
00:21:19,878 --> 00:21:21,038
promotional cost,

566
00:21:21,878 --> 00:21:23,278
and material cost will be deducted...

567
00:21:23,578 --> 00:21:26,378
to decide the top three teams who will survive.

568
00:21:26,548 --> 00:21:27,748
More than half will be eliminated.

569
00:21:28,248 --> 00:21:31,218
However, until the business ends,

570
00:21:31,788 --> 00:21:35,288
your material costs will not be revealed to each other.

571
00:21:36,088 --> 00:21:37,328
It won't be revealed?

572
00:21:37,328 --> 00:21:39,128
I thought they'd reveal it at the start.

573
00:21:39,458 --> 00:21:41,668
They won't tell us how much in the negative we're starting from.

574
00:21:41,668 --> 00:21:43,068
(The teams' starting sales won't be revealed.)

575
00:21:43,768 --> 00:21:45,468
The material cost could become a variable.

576
00:21:45,868 --> 00:21:47,738
Also, the sales...

577
00:21:48,208 --> 00:21:50,868
will change based on the customer ratings.

578
00:21:51,008 --> 00:21:52,138
- What?
- Customer ratings?

579
00:21:52,138 --> 00:21:53,878
- Based on the customer ratings?
- If your average ratings...

580
00:21:54,038 --> 00:21:58,478
is 5, your sales will be 150 percent of the total sales.

581
00:21:58,478 --> 00:21:59,918
(Average ratings of 5: 150 percent of the total sales)

582
00:21:59,918 --> 00:22:03,888
If you get 4 stars, it will be 125 percent of the total sales.

583
00:22:04,218 --> 00:22:07,418
If you get 3 stars, it will be 100 percent of the total sales.

584
00:22:07,688 --> 00:22:09,788
You're at the baseline when you get three stars.

585
00:22:10,528 --> 00:22:12,828
If you get two stars, it will be...

586
00:22:12,828 --> 00:22:14,558
- This changes a lot of things.
- seventy-five percent.

587
00:22:15,228 --> 00:22:17,968
If you get one star,

588
00:22:18,898 --> 00:22:20,338
only 50 percent of the sales...

589
00:22:20,668 --> 00:22:22,968
- will be reflected.
- The customer ratings are crucial.

590
00:22:23,208 --> 00:22:24,438
That's half gone.

591
00:22:25,978 --> 00:22:27,708
There's a variable.

592
00:22:27,708 --> 00:22:29,278
(The customer ratings weightage has become a lot stronger.)

593
00:22:29,948 --> 00:22:33,148
Now, I'll reveal your new restaurants...

594
00:22:33,478 --> 00:22:36,048
and the amount to be deducted.

595
00:22:36,488 --> 00:22:37,518
Goodness.

596
00:22:37,648 --> 00:22:39,358
(Order kiosk)

597
00:22:39,358 --> 00:22:40,388
Kim Hoon.

598
00:22:42,888 --> 00:22:46,128
Chef's Cooking Makes Us Happy.

599
00:22:47,158 --> 00:22:50,028
Chef's meat-packed kimchi stew.

600
00:22:51,068 --> 00:22:52,768
Rental fee, 400 dollars.

601
00:22:52,938 --> 00:22:55,368
Promotional cost, 320 dollars.

602
00:22:55,768 --> 00:22:58,338
The total deduction is 720 dollars.

603
00:22:58,338 --> 00:22:59,738
(Total: Minus 720 dollars)

604
00:23:00,078 --> 00:23:01,708
What? Kimchi stew?

605
00:23:01,708 --> 00:23:03,248
- Kimchi stew?
- Kimchi stew?

606
00:23:03,248 --> 00:23:04,408
What?

607
00:23:05,048 --> 00:23:06,418
Eat And Flight.

608
00:23:06,848 --> 00:23:08,018
- Three?
- Three?

609
00:23:08,788 --> 00:23:10,118
(Premium dried pollack hangover soup set)

610
00:23:10,118 --> 00:23:11,188
What's that?

611
00:23:11,188 --> 00:23:12,518
They have kimchi stew.

612
00:23:12,518 --> 00:23:13,618
They have beef soup too.

613
00:23:14,488 --> 00:23:17,488
- What?
- It's a shame our menus overlap,

614
00:23:17,758 --> 00:23:19,828
but we use black pork.

615
00:23:20,598 --> 00:23:22,768
Total deduction, 500 dollars.

616
00:23:22,768 --> 00:23:23,898
(Jung Ho Young, Eat And Flight, Total: Minus 500 dollars for rent)

617
00:23:24,398 --> 00:23:27,498
- Lee Sung Hoon, Good Morning Earth.
- It looks good.

618
00:23:27,498 --> 00:23:28,508
Koony.

619
00:23:28,508 --> 00:23:31,738
Hong Seok Cheon, Itaewon Class Thai.

620
00:23:33,238 --> 00:23:34,378
Choi Sang Hyun.

621
00:23:34,978 --> 00:23:36,208
Spring Beef Bone Soup Ready...

622
00:23:36,208 --> 00:23:37,448
- in 5 Minutes.
- In 5 minutes.

623
00:23:37,978 --> 00:23:40,948
Total deduction, 650 dollars.

624
00:23:40,948 --> 00:23:42,488
(Choi Sang Hyun, total: Minus 650 dollars)

625
00:23:43,118 --> 00:23:44,288
We must serve our food in five minutes.

626
00:23:44,958 --> 00:23:47,658
Kim Ho Yoon, total deduction.

627
00:23:48,588 --> 00:23:50,158
It's 1,220 dollars.

628
00:23:50,158 --> 00:23:51,998
(Kim Ho Yoon, 1,220 dollars)

629
00:23:51,998 --> 00:23:53,828
(Rent: 600 dollars, promotional cost: 620 dollars)

630
00:23:53,828 --> 00:23:56,628
That's a lot. Is he rich?

631
00:23:57,068 --> 00:23:58,338
I thought they'd place last.

632
00:23:58,538 --> 00:24:00,738
No way can they rank in the top three.

633
00:24:01,268 --> 00:24:02,468
Ho Yoon, will you be okay?

634
00:24:03,608 --> 00:24:04,768
It was fine.

635
00:24:06,478 --> 00:24:09,008
All the top seven contestants are the best of the professionals.

636
00:24:09,008 --> 00:24:11,378
We'll compensate our shortcomings...

637
00:24:11,378 --> 00:24:13,948
by buying the banner slots and providing customers information.

638
00:24:14,648 --> 00:24:16,318
You should take your mom with you.

639
00:24:16,318 --> 00:24:17,388
(Mom couldn't prepare it for you. As a chef, I will!)

640
00:24:17,388 --> 00:24:19,718
The banners are significant.

641
00:24:20,488 --> 00:24:24,158
I was very jealous of Chef Kim Ho Yoon's banners.

642
00:24:24,328 --> 00:24:27,098
Take this to your house.

643
00:24:28,198 --> 00:24:29,228
The last one.

644
00:24:29,568 --> 00:24:31,398
It's just too crowded here.

645
00:24:31,768 --> 00:24:33,368
(Lee Yeon Bok, the Masked Noodle King)

646
00:24:33,368 --> 00:24:36,408
Lee Yeon Bok, rental fee is ten dollars.

647
00:24:36,908 --> 00:24:38,538
- Ten dollars?
- Ten dollars.

648
00:24:38,538 --> 00:24:41,478
(Lee Yeon Bok, rental fee 10 dollars)

649
00:24:41,648 --> 00:24:42,948
That's crazy cheap.

650
00:24:43,248 --> 00:24:46,248
The LED video at the entrance, 250 dollars.

651
00:24:46,448 --> 00:24:47,618
My gosh.

652
00:24:47,618 --> 00:24:49,148
(Lee Yeon Bok, the Masked Noodle King: Minus 250 dollars)

653
00:24:49,148 --> 00:24:50,618
- It's eye-catching.
- It's eye-catching.

654
00:24:50,748 --> 00:24:52,558
You can see it as soon as you come up.

655
00:24:52,558 --> 00:24:54,658
(Food court)

656
00:24:54,918 --> 00:24:56,788
The other banners are like,

657
00:24:56,788 --> 00:24:59,798
"What's this piece of paper?"

658
00:24:59,798 --> 00:25:02,168
I only had my eyes on this from the very beginning.

659
00:25:02,498 --> 00:25:05,198
If you guys kept bidding, I'd have bid 1,000 dollars on it.

660
00:25:05,838 --> 00:25:07,368
Ho Yoon.

661
00:25:07,368 --> 00:25:08,508
Bring it here.

662
00:25:09,268 --> 00:25:10,368
What?

663
00:25:10,938 --> 00:25:13,138
- Put the banners there.
- Three banners?

664
00:25:13,138 --> 00:25:14,138
(The banners can be placed anywhere.)

665
00:25:14,138 --> 00:25:16,808
It's Chinese, it looks Chinese,

666
00:25:16,908 --> 00:25:19,748
and there's a video, so it looks very dynamic.

667
00:25:19,878 --> 00:25:21,378
It made you want to eat it.

668
00:25:21,888 --> 00:25:23,348
(Hororok Samgye Soft Tofu, Eat And Flight,)

669
00:25:23,348 --> 00:25:24,788
(Good Morning Earth, Itaewon Class Thai)

670
00:25:24,788 --> 00:25:25,888
Everyone prepared so well.

671
00:25:26,258 --> 00:25:28,018
- Everyone keeps improving, right?
- Exactly.

672
00:25:28,688 --> 00:25:29,688
I don't know.

673
00:25:30,388 --> 00:25:32,928
The business opens...

674
00:25:32,928 --> 00:25:34,828
- from 6am to 9am.
- For 3 hours.

675
00:25:35,398 --> 00:25:36,668
That's crazy.

676
00:25:37,728 --> 00:25:41,168
In this mission, you can get...

677
00:25:41,168 --> 00:25:43,008
one part-timer.

678
00:25:43,008 --> 00:25:44,268
(Each team got their part-timer.)

679
00:25:44,268 --> 00:25:46,538
Now, please start preparing...

680
00:25:46,538 --> 00:25:49,208
for the airport's morning business.

681
00:25:49,408 --> 00:25:53,018
(Time until the business starts)

682
00:25:53,478 --> 00:25:54,818
What I'm worried about is...

683
00:25:55,348 --> 00:25:57,788
for the burners and stuff,

684
00:25:57,788 --> 00:26:00,658
we need to compete... Rather than compete...

685
00:26:01,018 --> 00:26:02,328
We need to share them.

686
00:26:02,458 --> 00:26:04,728
We needed to scramble for equipment.

687
00:26:04,728 --> 00:26:05,898
It was a hectic war.

688
00:26:06,728 --> 00:26:09,328
That was too much.

689
00:26:09,898 --> 00:26:13,268
(The food court has 7 kitchens.)

690
00:26:13,398 --> 00:26:16,768
(All the kitchens connect to...)

691
00:26:16,768 --> 00:26:19,378
(communal kitchens.)

692
00:26:19,778 --> 00:26:22,948
(The communal kitchens, which look like a maze...)

693
00:26:24,448 --> 00:26:29,018
(Kitchen 1)

694
00:26:31,348 --> 00:26:35,058
(Kitchen 2)

695
00:26:36,358 --> 00:26:38,998
(There are only two communal kitchens.)

696
00:26:39,328 --> 00:26:41,458
(From the basic pots...)

697
00:26:41,458 --> 00:26:43,598
(to various pails)

698
00:26:43,898 --> 00:26:47,268
(Even big cauldrons and burners)

699
00:26:47,768 --> 00:26:51,108
(Every team has to share the communal kitchens.)

700
00:26:51,708 --> 00:26:56,178
(Who will secure it first?)

701
00:26:57,248 --> 00:27:00,948
(Kim Hoon is the first to enter the communal kitchen.)

702
00:27:00,948 --> 00:27:02,748
I need to take them.

703
00:27:03,648 --> 00:27:04,748
I need to take them quickly.

704
00:27:05,318 --> 00:27:07,588
What's this? It's too narrow.

705
00:27:07,588 --> 00:27:09,558
(Jong In on his team use the bypath to check out the restaurant.)

706
00:27:09,788 --> 00:27:11,588
Jong In, that fool, where did he go?

707
00:27:14,458 --> 00:27:15,868
Take the equipment quickly.

708
00:27:15,868 --> 00:27:19,368
(He takes everything he can find.)

709
00:27:20,638 --> 00:27:22,938
A few pots... I needed them to boil broths,

710
00:27:22,938 --> 00:27:24,508
but there weren't many.

711
00:27:26,238 --> 00:27:29,548
(The big pails aren't in abundance.)

712
00:27:29,978 --> 00:27:34,048
(Kim Hoon and Kim Jong In quickly take the pails.)

713
00:27:34,048 --> 00:27:35,048
Hey.

714
00:27:35,048 --> 00:27:37,948
Are they using the pots?

715
00:27:38,558 --> 00:27:40,988
(Surprised)

716
00:27:41,058 --> 00:27:42,888
These jerks are already taking them.

717
00:27:42,888 --> 00:27:44,158
(Jung Ho Young and Song Hoon are one step behind.)

718
00:27:45,198 --> 00:27:46,198
That...

719
00:27:46,398 --> 00:27:47,728
I kept it aside for myself.

720
00:27:47,728 --> 00:27:48,928
- This?
- Yes.

721
00:27:49,428 --> 00:27:51,468
(Returning)

722
00:27:51,868 --> 00:27:54,768
(Song Hoon secures the remaining pails.)

723
00:27:55,138 --> 00:27:56,168
This...

724
00:28:01,878 --> 00:28:03,948
We need to secure here first.

725
00:28:04,408 --> 00:28:06,618
(They pour the meat into the communal pot.)

726
00:28:06,618 --> 00:28:07,818
Done.

727
00:28:08,048 --> 00:28:10,788
- Put it here first.
- Okay.

728
00:28:11,488 --> 00:28:13,088
There were two big pots.

729
00:28:13,088 --> 00:28:16,488
One already had meat inside.

730
00:28:17,258 --> 00:28:19,158
- Whose meat is that?
- Ours.

731
00:28:19,158 --> 00:28:20,728
When will you finish using it?

732
00:28:20,728 --> 00:28:22,368
We'll need to use it for a long time.

733
00:28:22,728 --> 00:28:24,498
I just need to boil chicken.

734
00:28:24,498 --> 00:28:26,338
We have no burner inside.

735
00:28:26,438 --> 00:28:27,938
This is the only burner.

736
00:28:30,568 --> 00:28:32,878
I should've thrown some chicken inside first.

737
00:28:33,508 --> 00:28:35,008
The veterans sure are different.

738
00:28:35,948 --> 00:28:37,708
I felt a bit bad,

739
00:28:38,008 --> 00:28:40,818
but we had no choice but to use that burner.

740
00:28:41,118 --> 00:28:44,488
(While they're fighting over the big pot on one side...)

741
00:28:44,648 --> 00:28:47,088
(The other communal kitchen)

742
00:28:50,658 --> 00:28:53,628
(Yu Tae Hui spots a blender.)

743
00:28:58,268 --> 00:29:02,008
(Lee Sung Hoon takes a food pan.)

744
00:29:02,308 --> 00:29:05,978
We were quiet but fast.

745
00:29:05,978 --> 00:29:08,138
We went in fast and left quickly.

746
00:29:09,478 --> 00:29:12,948
I've walked around with no presence many times already,

747
00:29:13,178 --> 00:29:15,148
so I went inside with no presence from the start.

748
00:29:15,148 --> 00:29:16,318
(Lee Sung Hoon quietly took the equipment.)

749
00:29:19,858 --> 00:29:21,418
So I took a lot.

750
00:29:21,418 --> 00:29:24,458
(Thanks to that, they managed to secure enough equipment.)

751
00:29:24,928 --> 00:29:26,828
- That's enough food pans, right?
- Yes, that's enough.

752
00:29:28,668 --> 00:29:30,328
Place small equipment here.

753
00:29:30,328 --> 00:29:31,898
(Team Lee Sung Hoon quietly finishes preparing.)

754
00:29:31,898 --> 00:29:33,838
We were practically ninjas.

755
00:29:35,868 --> 00:29:37,308
(Exclaiming)

756
00:29:37,308 --> 00:29:40,138
I might get lost halfway.

757
00:29:40,678 --> 00:29:44,608
(Team Lee Yeon Bok arrives a lot later than the others.)

758
00:29:44,608 --> 00:29:46,648
We still haven't reached the communal kitchen?

759
00:29:48,518 --> 00:29:50,648
It feels farther than when we checked last time.

760
00:29:51,088 --> 00:29:52,288
Why does it feel so far?

761
00:29:52,788 --> 00:29:55,958
(Unlike other kitchens gathered in the hall...)

762
00:29:56,488 --> 00:30:00,428
The kitchen is one thing, but it's a kitchen in exile.

763
00:30:00,998 --> 00:30:03,028
It's all the way in the corner.

764
00:30:03,028 --> 00:30:04,498
(Yeon Bok's kitchen is in the corner of the food court.)

765
00:30:04,628 --> 00:30:05,798
It's not connected.

766
00:30:06,698 --> 00:30:07,868
It's not connected.

767
00:30:08,238 --> 00:30:09,838
(Kitchens A, B, C)

768
00:30:09,838 --> 00:30:11,638
(Kitchens D, E, F)

769
00:30:11,638 --> 00:30:12,978
We need to exit here?

770
00:30:12,978 --> 00:30:14,138
(The way to the communal kitchen is behind the restaurant.)

771
00:30:14,138 --> 00:30:15,708
- Like this.
- Oh, my gosh.

772
00:30:16,178 --> 00:30:17,748
Which way?

773
00:30:17,748 --> 00:30:20,348
We might get lost when we get really busy.

774
00:30:20,548 --> 00:30:21,678
It wasn't even a straight line.

775
00:30:21,678 --> 00:30:23,648
The path was like a maze.

776
00:30:23,648 --> 00:30:24,888
It's this far?

777
00:30:25,318 --> 00:30:26,388
This is bad.

778
00:30:30,488 --> 00:30:31,758
- Here, right?
- Yes.

779
00:30:32,028 --> 00:30:34,958
Look for a pail which can be used to boil broth.

780
00:30:36,998 --> 00:30:41,498
(Team Lee Yeon Bok quickly starts looking for a pail.)

781
00:30:42,408 --> 00:30:43,638
There's a big one.

782
00:30:43,638 --> 00:30:45,338
(But this section's pails...)

783
00:30:46,238 --> 00:30:48,708
Take this.

784
00:30:48,708 --> 00:30:50,508
(were all taken by Team Choi Sang Hyun.)

785
00:30:52,548 --> 00:30:54,378
- This.
- Is this the only one?

786
00:30:54,378 --> 00:30:55,918
- Yes.
- This isn't enough.

787
00:30:56,018 --> 00:30:58,188
- This... Hold on.
- It's too small.

788
00:30:58,788 --> 00:31:02,288
(The other teams have taken all the important equipment.)

789
00:31:02,528 --> 00:31:04,888
- A big pail...
- A pail.

790
00:31:09,528 --> 00:31:10,628
Hold on.

791
00:31:11,528 --> 00:31:12,538
Yes.

792
00:31:12,538 --> 00:31:14,338
Byeong Ho, come here. Can we use this?

793
00:31:14,568 --> 00:31:17,568
(He spots another big pot.)

794
00:31:17,638 --> 00:31:20,808
- Yes.
- They say to use it by agreement.

795
00:31:22,108 --> 00:31:23,548
Let's call dibs on this.

796
00:31:23,548 --> 00:31:25,048
We must take this.

797
00:31:25,048 --> 00:31:26,618
(Team Lee Yeon Bok secures a huge empty pot.)

798
00:31:26,718 --> 00:31:30,288
Even when we didn't use it, we filled it up with water.

799
00:31:31,988 --> 00:31:34,618
I didn't want the others to take it when it became empty.

800
00:31:34,688 --> 00:31:37,228
(It's a battle zone, everyone on alert for a chance.)

801
00:31:37,228 --> 00:31:40,398
It was complete chaos.

802
00:31:40,398 --> 00:31:41,858
It's a war.

803
00:31:45,598 --> 00:31:47,298
There's no pail.

804
00:31:47,298 --> 00:31:48,908
Exactly. We don't have something like this.

805
00:31:50,438 --> 00:31:53,378
(The other teams have secured the pails.)

806
00:31:53,678 --> 00:31:55,078
Look. Those pails...

807
00:31:55,408 --> 00:31:56,778
How did you take them?

808
00:31:56,778 --> 00:31:58,008
Are there more pails?

809
00:31:58,008 --> 00:31:59,818
It's him again.

810
00:32:02,388 --> 00:32:05,588
That team took all the pails.

811
00:32:05,588 --> 00:32:06,818
Give us one pail.

812
00:32:07,358 --> 00:32:09,428
Isn't taking three pails too much?

813
00:32:09,828 --> 00:32:10,828
Sorry?

814
00:32:13,058 --> 00:32:14,828
Will you keep using the pail?

815
00:32:15,428 --> 00:32:16,568
Do you need to keep using it?

816
00:32:16,568 --> 00:32:20,598
If we can use that, I can give you this.

817
00:32:20,598 --> 00:32:22,608
We took this because we didn't have a pail.

818
00:32:24,068 --> 00:32:25,338
We have no burner at all.

819
00:32:25,338 --> 00:32:29,308
If you're done using it, we can exchange.

820
00:32:29,348 --> 00:32:31,478
- If you're done using it...
- We won't be exchanging it.

821
00:32:31,748 --> 00:32:33,218
Because my kitchen has no burner,

822
00:32:33,478 --> 00:32:36,318
we need to move back and forth, all the while boiling broth here.

823
00:32:38,018 --> 00:32:40,688
"You have 3? Then give us 1."

824
00:32:40,688 --> 00:32:42,458
And they asked for the big pot.

825
00:32:43,028 --> 00:32:45,428
We couldn't come to an agreement,

826
00:32:45,958 --> 00:32:48,398
so I said sorry...

827
00:32:48,398 --> 00:32:49,798
and went back to work.

828
00:32:55,768 --> 00:32:56,808
You don't use this, right?

829
00:32:57,738 --> 00:32:58,908
No, not now.

830
00:32:59,608 --> 00:33:00,838
Save it.

831
00:33:01,538 --> 00:33:02,778
Or they'll take it again.

832
00:33:02,778 --> 00:33:03,808
This...

833
00:33:03,808 --> 00:33:04,808
(You must take it first, or it will be taken.)

834
00:33:04,808 --> 00:33:06,178
- Low flame?
- Yes.

835
00:33:06,678 --> 00:33:08,478
Securing a spot is a fight too.

836
00:33:10,588 --> 00:33:13,658
(As the battle for cooking stations rages on,)

837
00:33:13,658 --> 00:33:16,688
(following the battle over equipment...)

838
00:33:18,828 --> 00:33:20,198
Will you be parboiling your abalones?

839
00:33:20,328 --> 00:33:21,328
Yes.

840
00:33:21,628 --> 00:33:23,568
Can I parboil mine with yours?

841
00:33:23,768 --> 00:33:24,928
- What?
- Can I parboil our abalones...

842
00:33:24,928 --> 00:33:26,068
with yours?

843
00:33:26,538 --> 00:33:28,198
Before you dump the water after taking the abalones out.

844
00:33:28,738 --> 00:33:29,738
Well...

845
00:33:29,938 --> 00:33:31,568
- Okay.
- We don't have a pot to do that.

846
00:33:32,978 --> 00:33:37,078
(Successfully parboiled abalones in Yeon Bok's pot)

847
00:33:37,378 --> 00:33:38,918
Abalones are done. All that's left is the chicken.

848
00:33:38,918 --> 00:33:39,978
Where do we boil it?

849
00:33:39,978 --> 00:33:41,448
We'll boil it here.

850
00:33:41,718 --> 00:33:42,888
But the broth.

851
00:33:43,718 --> 00:33:45,618
All that's left is the low stove.

852
00:33:46,988 --> 00:33:49,628
(The stove is already packed.)

853
00:33:50,188 --> 00:33:51,988
(Wandering around Yeon Bok again)

854
00:33:51,988 --> 00:33:52,998
So...

855
00:33:53,158 --> 00:33:54,398
Let's use a tray.

856
00:33:56,168 --> 00:33:57,368
- What is it?
- Let me fill it up...

857
00:33:57,368 --> 00:33:58,428
with new water to parboil the chicken.

858
00:33:59,198 --> 00:34:00,668
That's all you'll do, right?

859
00:34:00,668 --> 00:34:01,798
Yes, I won't boil the soup here.

860
00:34:01,998 --> 00:34:03,008
Okay.

861
00:34:03,068 --> 00:34:04,368
We need to use it right away.

862
00:34:04,368 --> 00:34:06,138
Got it. Parboiling the chicken is all I'll do.

863
00:34:06,508 --> 00:34:10,408
(Succesfully parboiled the chicken in Yeon Bok's pot)

864
00:34:10,678 --> 00:34:11,878
I'll empty the pot and wash it.

865
00:34:12,078 --> 00:34:13,978
Don't throw it away. Leave it.

866
00:34:14,978 --> 00:34:16,488
- Should I leave it?
- Yes.

867
00:34:16,818 --> 00:34:17,918
Let's use it as broth.

868
00:34:19,158 --> 00:34:20,218
Chicken broth?

869
00:34:20,218 --> 00:34:21,488
Yes, as chicken broth.

870
00:34:21,788 --> 00:34:23,528
- I'm sure it's rich.
- Good.

871
00:34:23,888 --> 00:34:27,628
(What's the menu Team Yeon Bok prepared today?)

872
00:34:28,198 --> 00:34:30,728
Fire is everything when it comes to Chinese cuisine.

873
00:34:31,428 --> 00:34:34,768
It's cooked to perfection only under high heat.

874
00:34:35,298 --> 00:34:38,238
There weren't any stoves in the kitchen.

875
00:34:38,468 --> 00:34:41,738
No stove really shocked me.

876
00:34:42,848 --> 00:34:44,308
(A corner kitchen won with 10 dollars)

877
00:34:44,308 --> 00:34:46,378
(Key feature: No stovetop)

878
00:34:46,618 --> 00:34:48,578
Even paying ten dollars for it felt like a waste.

879
00:34:48,778 --> 00:34:50,948
It should've been offered for free.

880
00:34:51,118 --> 00:34:52,558
Or an additional 200 dollars...

881
00:34:52,688 --> 00:34:55,218
should've been offered to the team that uses it.

882
00:34:55,218 --> 00:34:56,228
- Yes.
- That should've been the condition.

883
00:34:56,228 --> 00:34:58,688
Exactly. It was so inadequate that the kitchen...

884
00:34:58,688 --> 00:35:00,328
- felt like a penalty.
- Yes, a penalty.

885
00:35:00,498 --> 00:35:03,998
(A strategic choice, but unfavorable conditions)

886
00:35:04,328 --> 00:35:06,298
This is to cook jeon.

887
00:35:06,838 --> 00:35:08,168
- Right?
- Griddle.

888
00:35:08,638 --> 00:35:11,408
That was the only equipment we could cook hot food.

889
00:35:12,678 --> 00:35:14,908
Wait, this is a slushie.

890
00:35:15,278 --> 00:35:16,978
- A slushie.
- It's not the frozen type, right?

891
00:35:17,578 --> 00:35:18,978
- Like a slush.
- Yes.

892
00:35:18,978 --> 00:35:20,248
(And a cold broth machine)

893
00:35:20,248 --> 00:35:21,478
Like this?

894
00:35:22,288 --> 00:35:24,118
(All they have are a griddle and a cold broth machine.)

895
00:35:24,118 --> 00:35:26,818
Not having any stovetop is...

896
00:35:26,818 --> 00:35:28,318
(Yeon Bok's decision under such condition)

897
00:35:28,318 --> 00:35:30,088
During business...

898
00:35:31,788 --> 00:35:33,598
No fire?

899
00:35:34,198 --> 00:35:36,068
Then let's go with an ice-cold menu.

900
00:35:37,128 --> 00:35:39,338
If you watch those coming to the airport,

901
00:35:39,798 --> 00:35:41,298
some come in rushing,

902
00:35:41,298 --> 00:35:43,168
carry heavy suitcases, and such,

903
00:35:43,408 --> 00:35:44,908
making them all hot and sweaty.

904
00:35:45,908 --> 00:35:47,878
So the menu we chose was...

905
00:35:48,108 --> 00:35:49,348
Chinese-style naengmyeon.

906
00:35:49,908 --> 00:35:51,178
Let's try naengmyeon.

907
00:35:51,378 --> 00:35:52,918
We boldly chose naengmyeon.

908
00:35:53,278 --> 00:35:54,948
(Chinese-style naengmyeon)

909
00:35:54,948 --> 00:35:56,918
(Served in an icy broth with seafood,)

910
00:35:56,918 --> 00:35:58,848
(vegetables, and peanut butter)

911
00:35:59,318 --> 00:36:01,918
On top of the naengmyeon are abalone, jellyfish,

912
00:36:01,918 --> 00:36:03,058
and shrimp.

913
00:36:07,658 --> 00:36:09,998
It's a luxurious and hearty meal.

914
00:36:09,998 --> 00:36:12,798
(Chinese-style abalone naengmyeon)

915
00:36:13,468 --> 00:36:14,738
(Prepping 6 hours before business)

916
00:36:14,738 --> 00:36:16,768
Find a cooking station.

917
00:36:17,068 --> 00:36:19,808
(300 servings worth of shrimp)

918
00:36:21,908 --> 00:36:23,908
(2 boxes of abalone, a total of 310)

919
00:36:24,848 --> 00:36:28,318
(Prepared more than 300 servings of seafood)

920
00:36:29,218 --> 00:36:31,248
Time is literally flying. This is bad.

921
00:36:31,248 --> 00:36:34,758
(Turning on the heat of the only stovetop and big pot)

922
00:36:34,918 --> 00:36:36,728
- Pour both in.
- All together?

923
00:36:36,728 --> 00:36:37,828
Yes, all together.

924
00:36:40,658 --> 00:36:42,228
In the big pot,

925
00:36:42,568 --> 00:36:45,568
we were going to stir-fry, parboil, and boil.

926
00:36:50,038 --> 00:36:51,708
Shucking the abalone takes the whole day.

927
00:36:52,538 --> 00:36:54,378
This is practically a banquet hall.

928
00:36:54,578 --> 00:36:55,578
You're right.

929
00:36:56,408 --> 00:36:59,178
It's like making a 300-serving banquet with 3 people.

930
00:37:00,148 --> 00:37:02,018
Since we sell out really fast,

931
00:37:02,118 --> 00:37:04,748
let's try and sell as many as we can this time.

932
00:37:05,118 --> 00:37:06,358
(During Round 1)

933
00:37:06,358 --> 00:37:07,958
(We'll be out of mianbao xia in no time.)

934
00:37:08,158 --> 00:37:10,828
(Short of mianbao xia)

935
00:37:10,988 --> 00:37:12,328
(During Round 2)

936
00:37:12,328 --> 00:37:13,628
(Oh, no. I'm not sure if we can serve all the orders.)

937
00:37:13,628 --> 00:37:15,398
(We have about 10 servings left.)

938
00:37:15,628 --> 00:37:17,128
(But 10 isn't enough.)

939
00:37:17,598 --> 00:37:21,098
(Sold out early again due to not enough quantity)

940
00:37:21,638 --> 00:37:24,668
Customers really flock to the food court.

941
00:37:25,368 --> 00:37:28,338
Sell 300 servings, and we'll definitely win.

942
00:37:28,938 --> 00:37:29,978
That's what I think.

943
00:37:30,878 --> 00:37:32,048
The shrimp is good.

944
00:37:32,178 --> 00:37:33,178
(Parboiled all seafood)

945
00:37:33,178 --> 00:37:34,378
It's been perfectly parboiled.

946
00:37:34,748 --> 00:37:36,118
- The shrimp is plump.
- Right?

947
00:37:38,118 --> 00:37:39,418
Let's move on to the next step.

948
00:37:40,018 --> 00:37:43,358
(Abalone, squid, carrots, egg garnish)

949
00:37:43,588 --> 00:37:47,398
(Cutting up 300 servings worth of toppings)

950
00:37:47,598 --> 00:37:50,728
(Done setting up the toppings in perfect uniform)

951
00:37:51,268 --> 00:37:52,798
What? It's already past 2am?

952
00:37:53,298 --> 00:37:54,468
- Yes.
- Gosh.

953
00:37:54,468 --> 00:37:56,238
Time goes by so fast. We're doomed.

954
00:37:56,238 --> 00:37:57,568
(The reason Yeon Bok is in a rush is that...)

955
00:37:57,608 --> 00:37:59,978
(today's menu isn't solely Chinese-style naengmyeon.)

956
00:37:59,978 --> 00:38:01,778
Next to the Chinese-style naengmyeon...

957
00:38:01,778 --> 00:38:04,348
are yukjeon, zucchini jeon, and dumplings.

958
00:38:05,048 --> 00:38:07,578
Those three come as a meal.

959
00:38:07,578 --> 00:38:09,248
(Chinese-style naengmyeon with jeon and dumplings, 17.8 dollars)

960
00:38:10,988 --> 00:38:12,118
(Zucchini jeon, yukjeon)

961
00:38:12,118 --> 00:38:14,288
(Handmade dumplings)

962
00:38:14,518 --> 00:38:16,088
I'm known for dumplings.

963
00:38:16,088 --> 00:38:18,328
So today, we came in with a little cheat code.

964
00:38:18,588 --> 00:38:22,428
We'll feel relaxed once we get the dumplings done.

965
00:38:23,428 --> 00:38:24,868
Where are the eggs? 100 eggs.

966
00:38:25,268 --> 00:38:26,768
Let's fry them and then add them to the filling.

967
00:38:27,268 --> 00:38:28,538
It's so far away.

968
00:38:28,538 --> 00:38:30,138
This is practically a marathon.

969
00:38:36,108 --> 00:38:39,448
(Pouring in 100 eggs)

970
00:38:42,788 --> 00:38:43,788
What is that?

971
00:38:44,188 --> 00:38:45,788
- It's for the dumplings.
- Oh, my.

972
00:38:45,788 --> 00:38:47,758
We're making egg chive dumplings. This is the filling.

973
00:38:48,218 --> 00:38:50,088
Is that the filling for the dumplings?

974
00:38:50,328 --> 00:38:52,898
Yes, China has egg chive dumplings.

975
00:38:52,898 --> 00:38:54,928
That sounds delicious.

976
00:39:03,338 --> 00:39:06,508
(Eggs stir-fried over high heat)

977
00:39:06,608 --> 00:39:09,648
(Finely chopped chives)

978
00:39:11,778 --> 00:39:16,718
(Mix them together, and the dumpling filling is ready.)

979
00:39:18,118 --> 00:39:21,988
(Even the dumpling skins are made from scratch.)

980
00:39:26,228 --> 00:39:28,498
From the skin to the filling,

981
00:39:28,498 --> 00:39:30,798
the dumplings are wrapped and handmade right here.

982
00:39:37,668 --> 00:39:41,308
(Hand-shaping them carefully)

983
00:39:41,408 --> 00:39:42,608
Place the wrapped ones here.

984
00:39:42,608 --> 00:39:45,008
Wrap, griddle, and repeat. We'll cook them as we go.

985
00:39:46,018 --> 00:39:49,688
(The handmade dumplings are placed one at a time on the griddle.)

986
00:39:58,488 --> 00:40:02,598
(Time is flying towards the opening hour, 6am.)

987
00:40:02,868 --> 00:40:03,868
It's 4am.

988
00:40:04,698 --> 00:40:05,828
- What?
- It's 4am.

989
00:40:06,168 --> 00:40:07,168
Is it?

990
00:40:07,268 --> 00:40:08,768
(After making dumplings for 2 hours)

991
00:40:08,768 --> 00:40:09,868
Is this the second row?

992
00:40:10,008 --> 00:40:11,508
- Third row.
- Third? How many are there?

993
00:40:11,508 --> 00:40:13,808
Each row has 30, so a total of 90.

994
00:40:14,038 --> 00:40:15,038
Ninety.

995
00:40:16,108 --> 00:40:19,518
From what I see, we should reduce our target servings to 200.

996
00:40:20,118 --> 00:40:21,818
We also have jeon to cook.

997
00:40:22,178 --> 00:40:25,788
(Will they be ready in 2 hours?)

998
00:40:26,288 --> 00:40:28,888
I'll start cooking the kimchi stew fast.

999
00:40:28,888 --> 00:40:31,128
Okay, I'm going to cut the dried pollack.

1000
00:40:31,428 --> 00:40:34,498
- The radish can wait.
- Yes.

1001
00:40:34,798 --> 00:40:36,098
The customers are going overseas.

1002
00:40:36,368 --> 00:40:38,268
Whether they're traveling...

1003
00:40:38,268 --> 00:40:39,768
or studying abroad,

1004
00:40:39,968 --> 00:40:42,438
they leave for various reasons.

1005
00:40:43,268 --> 00:40:46,308
Leaving after having a hot, hearty meal...

1006
00:40:46,308 --> 00:40:47,908
seemed like a good idea.

1007
00:40:48,078 --> 00:40:49,108
(Eat And Flight)

1008
00:40:49,108 --> 00:40:51,678
Eat And Flight.

1009
00:40:52,248 --> 00:40:54,948
Why make kimchi stew when they are Japanese and Western cuisine chefs?

1010
00:40:54,948 --> 00:40:56,088
Weird.

1011
00:40:57,018 --> 00:40:59,088
I specialize in Japanese cuisine.

1012
00:40:59,358 --> 00:41:01,558
But my mom ran a Korean restaurant...

1013
00:41:01,558 --> 00:41:03,088
for over 40 years.

1014
00:41:03,188 --> 00:41:04,288
(On the day of the auction)

1015
00:41:04,288 --> 00:41:05,358
What's calling you right away?

1016
00:41:05,358 --> 00:41:07,128
- For breakfast.
- Honestly, 1 or 2.

1017
00:41:08,358 --> 00:41:11,068
(Out of the 7 food stations)

1018
00:41:11,098 --> 00:41:12,128
Stations A or B.

1019
00:41:12,128 --> 00:41:15,238
(A and B sell traditional Korean food.)

1020
00:41:15,468 --> 00:41:16,638
What about the foreign customers?

1021
00:41:16,638 --> 00:41:17,938
The foreign customers...

1022
00:41:18,108 --> 00:41:19,478
are leaving Korea.

1023
00:41:20,078 --> 00:41:21,978
They want Korean food for their last meal here.

1024
00:41:23,278 --> 00:41:24,378
When you go overseas,

1025
00:41:24,478 --> 00:41:27,348
the last meal you have is usually one of that country's.

1026
00:41:27,748 --> 00:41:28,778
Korean food.

1027
00:41:28,778 --> 00:41:29,888
(Korean food that works for all customers)

1028
00:41:29,888 --> 00:41:31,118
Korean food is the winning move.

1029
00:41:31,548 --> 00:41:32,758
No lose, just win.

1030
00:41:34,188 --> 00:41:35,688
The menu I thought of...

1031
00:41:35,688 --> 00:41:36,958
Because of these?

1032
00:41:37,428 --> 00:41:39,428
One main meal with three side dishes.

1033
00:41:39,798 --> 00:41:40,858
This is a rice bowl, right?

1034
00:41:42,398 --> 00:41:45,028
The earthen pot is the key to us.

1035
00:41:45,028 --> 00:41:46,068
(Using the earthen pot)

1036
00:41:46,268 --> 00:41:47,798
When it comes to breakfast,

1037
00:41:48,098 --> 00:41:49,338
warm dishes...

1038
00:41:49,908 --> 00:41:52,568
like soup and food served in broth are more likely to win...

1039
00:41:52,778 --> 00:41:53,978
than cold dishes.

1040
00:41:54,908 --> 00:41:57,348
The menu items we prepared are...

1041
00:41:58,008 --> 00:42:00,948
Korean beef soup set.

1042
00:42:01,078 --> 00:42:03,348
premium dried pollack hangover soup set,

1043
00:42:03,688 --> 00:42:06,258
and Jeju black pork kimchi stew set.

1044
00:42:06,458 --> 00:42:07,658
Those three.

1045
00:42:08,288 --> 00:42:11,428
