1623
01:05:54,052 --> 01:05:56,162
- We're in third place.
- What a relief.

1624
01:05:56,162 --> 01:05:57,732
I'm so relieved. We're in third place.

1625
01:05:58,032 --> 01:06:00,762
(The kimchi stew groups are currently in the lead.)

1626
01:06:00,962 --> 01:06:02,632
(1st: 359 dollars, 2nd: 312 dollars, 3rd: 231.4 dollars)

1627
01:06:02,632 --> 01:06:05,902
(Lee Yeon Bok begins a fierce pursuit in 3rd place.)

1628
01:06:06,732 --> 01:06:09,542
(The transit passengers who ordered the jjamppong set)

1629
01:06:10,072 --> 01:06:14,212
(Premium jjamppong set)

1630
01:06:14,942 --> 01:06:15,942
This is good.

1631
01:06:16,142 --> 01:06:17,212
Isn't it nice?

1632
01:06:17,812 --> 01:06:19,552
- Yes.
- It's really good.

1633
01:06:19,682 --> 01:06:21,622
(Slurping)

1634
01:06:23,652 --> 01:06:25,852
I can't believe this is just airport food.

1635
01:06:26,792 --> 01:06:28,262
Local Korean food must be amazing.

1636
01:06:28,262 --> 01:06:29,692
- Their street food.
- Yes.

1637
01:06:31,792 --> 01:06:34,462
Okay. I made up my mind after eating this.

1638
01:06:35,062 --> 01:06:38,172
I want to visit Korea again to properly enjoy the food.

1639
01:06:39,232 --> 01:06:40,602
How about you?

1640
01:06:41,842 --> 01:06:43,042
- Good?
- Great.

1641
01:06:43,472 --> 01:06:45,512
- This is really good.
- Do you like it?

1642
01:06:45,512 --> 01:06:47,942
(Lee Yeon Bok's jjamppong set, Jung Ho Young's kimchi stew)

1643
01:06:47,942 --> 01:06:49,342
- This is really good.
- But...

1644
01:06:51,382 --> 01:06:52,682
Good Morning Earth.

1645
01:06:54,622 --> 01:06:57,322
(A somewhat chilling good morning)

1646
01:06:58,222 --> 01:06:59,622
Our niche market strategy...

1647
01:07:00,022 --> 01:07:01,862
- needs to work.
- I know.

1648
01:07:02,562 --> 01:07:05,592
(Lee Sung Hoon won the bid for the hot dog station.)

1649
01:07:06,092 --> 01:07:07,932
(I bet this is a burger place.)

1650
01:07:07,932 --> 01:07:09,432
- Like patties.
- Right.

1651
01:07:09,632 --> 01:07:11,702
Let's avoid D. Not D.

1652
01:07:12,072 --> 01:07:13,732
I don't want this.

1653
01:07:14,472 --> 01:07:16,072
There will not be much we can do in D.

1654
01:07:16,842 --> 01:07:20,612
(The kitchen is tailored for fast food,)

1655
01:07:20,712 --> 01:07:23,742
(many of them wanted to avoid it.)

1656
01:07:24,512 --> 01:07:27,252
(Lee Sung Hoon won the hot dog station.)

1657
01:07:27,252 --> 01:07:29,422
(What is he going to make?)

1658
01:07:31,922 --> 01:07:33,192
This is actually better.

1659
01:07:34,322 --> 01:07:36,022
Even among the existing booths, the hot dog spot...

1660
01:07:36,022 --> 01:07:37,632
