1661
01:07:38,262 --> 01:07:40,162
Then we should do Western food here too.

1662
01:07:40,532 --> 01:07:42,232
Why don't we just focus...

1663
01:07:42,432 --> 01:07:43,862
entirely on foreign customers?

1664
01:07:44,472 --> 01:07:45,602
That's a good idea.

1665
01:07:45,602 --> 01:07:47,332
Because for foreigners,

1666
01:07:47,742 --> 01:07:49,102
- a grilled cheese sandwich...
- Yes.

1667
01:07:49,102 --> 01:07:51,142
is an absolute classic. And tomato soup.

1668
01:07:51,742 --> 01:07:52,772
That sounds good.

1669
01:07:56,282 --> 01:07:58,582
(Grilled sandwich)

1670
01:07:58,582 --> 01:07:59,612
(Grilled cheese sandwich)

1671
01:07:59,612 --> 01:08:00,682
(Grilled egg and cheese sandwich)

1672
01:08:00,682 --> 01:08:02,182
(Grilled ham and cheese sandwich)

1673
01:08:02,182 --> 01:08:04,082
We prepared sandwiches...

1674
01:08:04,122 --> 01:08:06,522
and set menus that include sandwiches.

1675
01:08:06,522 --> 01:08:09,162
(Grilled cheese sandwich set, 22 dollars)

1676
01:08:09,162 --> 01:08:11,892
It also includes hummus and salad inside.

1677
01:08:12,162 --> 01:08:13,592
We also included a fried egg...

1678
01:08:13,592 --> 01:08:15,832
and home fries, which are potatoes stir-fried with onions.

1679
01:08:16,562 --> 01:08:18,302
It comes with white ragu we made...

1680
01:08:18,302 --> 01:08:20,872
and a duxelles made with mushrooms.

1681
01:08:21,702 --> 01:08:22,942
(When the menu was revealed a while ago)

1682
01:08:23,702 --> 01:08:25,812
- What is this?
- Sandwich?

1683
01:08:26,572 --> 01:08:27,882
The ragu sounds good.

1684
01:08:28,142 --> 01:08:31,352
Their mouths were saying it looked good,

1685
01:08:31,752 --> 01:08:34,252
but their eyes were saying, "There goes one team."

1686
01:08:34,352 --> 01:08:37,792
Everyone's eyes looked so excited.

1687
01:08:37,792 --> 01:08:38,952
Like, "We will beat at least one team."

1688
01:08:39,292 --> 01:08:40,422
"We have at least one underneath us."

1689
01:08:43,162 --> 01:08:46,132
I honestly thought it was not a good idea.

1690
01:08:46,432 --> 01:08:47,832
You'd want a proper meal,

1691
01:08:47,832 --> 01:08:49,632
not just a sandwich.

1692
01:08:49,632 --> 01:08:51,132
Once you enter a food court.

1693
01:08:51,202 --> 01:08:53,702
I thought all the chefs here would cook Korean food.

1694
01:08:54,002 --> 01:08:55,802
We decided to switch our target entirely...

1695
01:08:55,802 --> 01:08:57,202
and focus on foreigners.

1696
01:08:57,542 --> 01:09:00,442
And instead of first place, we set our target ranking...

1697
01:09:00,642 --> 01:09:02,082
at third place.

1698
01:09:02,742 --> 01:09:05,012
We planned to aim for third place by targeting the niche market.

1699
01:09:05,012 --> 01:09:06,212
That was our plan.

1700
01:09:06,712 --> 01:09:08,122
Please let a lot of foreign customers come.

1701
01:09:08,122 --> 01:09:09,322
What if it just ends up staying as a niche?

1702
01:09:10,422 --> 01:09:12,992
We wanted to greet people with the feeling of welcoming...

1703
01:09:12,992 --> 01:09:14,562
all the mornings in the world.

1704
01:09:14,992 --> 01:09:18,432
That is why we came up with the name Good Morning Earth.

1705
01:09:18,732 --> 01:09:22,132
We want to approach foreigners in a more familiar way.

1706
01:09:23,002 --> 01:09:28,102
(Will the niche strategy targeting foreigners with Western food work?)

1707
01:09:28,872 --> 01:09:31,672
(Foreign customers enter right on cue time.)

1708
01:09:32,312 --> 01:09:34,172
I'm not sure.

1709
01:09:34,312 --> 01:09:35,342
Oh, yes.

1710
01:09:35,342 --> 01:09:39,052
(Approaching the kiosk to order)

1711
01:09:39,882 --> 01:09:42,882
I hope those foreign customers order ours.

1712
01:09:43,982 --> 01:09:44,992
Those two?

1713
01:09:45,222 --> 01:09:46,922
They already ordered. They have the receipt in hand,

1714
01:09:46,922 --> 01:09:47,962
