1715
01:09:48,992 --> 01:09:50,522
They are heading over to the far right.

1716
01:09:51,932 --> 01:09:54,092
(Passing right by Seok Cheon's team)

1717
01:09:54,862 --> 01:09:56,132
Hello.

1718
01:09:56,962 --> 01:10:01,032
(Lee Sung Hoon's restaurant)

1719
01:10:01,342 --> 01:10:03,102
(Good Morning Earth: 1 order)

1720
01:10:03,542 --> 01:10:04,572
Enjoy.

1721
01:10:04,572 --> 01:10:05,842
(Good Morning Earth: 2 orders)

1722
01:10:06,712 --> 01:10:09,912
(A family of foreign customers)

1723
01:10:10,512 --> 01:10:12,582
I think I'll have the white ragu.

1724
01:10:15,122 --> 01:10:18,592
(All members of the foreign family ordered sandwiches.)

1725
01:10:19,022 --> 01:10:22,092
(Another foreign customer is ordering right next to them.)

1726
01:10:22,092 --> 01:10:24,592
(Picking a sandwich)

1727
01:10:25,192 --> 01:10:26,362
(1 order)

1728
01:10:27,732 --> 01:10:29,202
Okay. One special set.

1729
01:10:29,462 --> 01:10:30,902
White ragu sandwich.

1730
01:10:30,902 --> 01:10:32,932
- Grilled ham and cheese sandwich.
- Okay.

1731
01:10:33,432 --> 01:10:35,742
- Have a nice trip. Thank you.
- The ragu is ready.

1732
01:10:36,642 --> 01:10:38,712
Hello. Your number, please.

1733
01:10:39,472 --> 01:10:41,942
(Good Morning Earth: 8 orders)

1734
01:10:42,642 --> 01:10:44,142
(Good Morning Earth: 9 orders)

1735
01:10:44,142 --> 01:10:45,452
Thank you. Enjoy.

1736
01:10:46,712 --> 01:10:49,522
(Out of 14 cumulative orders,)

1737
01:10:49,522 --> 01:10:50,552
(10 are from foreign customers.)

1738
01:10:50,552 --> 01:10:52,122
- Two ragus, right?
- Yes.

1739
01:10:54,122 --> 01:10:55,392
Hello.

1740
01:10:57,422 --> 01:10:59,332
Can you give it five minutes?

1741
01:10:59,632 --> 01:11:00,662
- Five minutes?
- Yes.

1742
01:11:00,662 --> 01:11:03,102
I'll get my bags from downstairs and come back.

1743
01:11:03,102 --> 01:11:04,502
Okay. Then, come back...

1744
01:11:04,502 --> 01:11:05,802
Sure. Okay.

1745
01:11:07,102 --> 01:11:08,242
- Hi.
- Hi.

1746
01:11:08,242 --> 01:11:11,942
Could you let me know where the sugar and creamer are?

1747
01:11:12,142 --> 01:11:14,042
(It's not easy to deal with foreign customers.)

1748
01:11:14,042 --> 01:11:16,212
Are you asking for the hall...

1749
01:11:16,442 --> 01:11:17,742
- Server?
- Server?

1750
01:11:17,742 --> 01:11:19,612
Sugar? Yes, and creamer.

1751
01:11:20,952 --> 01:11:23,982
(Succeeded in targeting foreign customers)

1752
01:11:23,982 --> 01:11:27,752
(Failed in handling foreign customers)

1753
01:11:28,022 --> 01:11:30,862
(Business isn't easy today as well.)

1754
01:11:30,922 --> 01:11:32,892
(The foreign family who ordered three kinds of sandwiches)

1755
01:11:32,892 --> 01:11:35,162
(Special set, white lagu sandwich, grilled ham and cheese sandwich)

1756
01:11:35,302 --> 01:11:37,762
You should try this. Give me half of that one.

1757
01:11:38,402 --> 01:11:40,702
(Splitting in half and sharing)

1758
01:11:40,702 --> 01:11:41,802
It's so good.

1759
01:11:44,512 --> 01:11:46,772
(Crunchy)

1760
01:11:52,112 --> 01:11:53,952
You like the sandwich, right? It was good.

1761
01:11:53,952 --> 01:11:54,982
Yes.

1762
01:11:55,722 --> 01:11:57,282
The ragu was delicious.

1763
01:11:57,482 --> 01:12:00,122
It tastes like a Philly cheesesteak.

1764
01:12:01,152 --> 01:12:02,762
It was a 5 out of 5.

1765
01:12:03,722 --> 01:12:07,792
(A special flavor compared to the other dishes eaten together)

1766
01:12:08,562 --> 01:12:11,032
- You want a piece of these?
- Sure.

1767
01:12:11,872 --> 01:12:14,032
Okay. Here we go.

1768
01:12:14,332 --> 01:12:16,042
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

1769
01:12:16,642 --> 01:12:19,272
(Crispy)

1770
01:12:19,442 --> 01:12:21,142
Pretty good. I feel like I've had it before.

1771
01:12:21,142 --> 01:12:22,212
Yes. It's good.

1772
01:12:23,242 --> 01:12:24,412
- Really good, though.
- Yes.

1773
01:12:24,552 --> 01:12:26,482
Five stars. A hundred percent.

1774
01:12:26,582 --> 01:12:29,282
Five. I want to bring more than five. Is that possible?

1775
01:12:30,822 --> 01:12:32,222
Please retrieve your card.

1776
01:12:32,692 --> 01:12:35,062
- There's still time left.
- What are you going to have?

1777
01:12:35,062 --> 01:12:36,322
Do you want to try one?

1778
01:12:36,662 --> 01:12:38,392
But we won't be able to finish everything.

1779
01:12:38,392 --> 01:12:40,232
- How about Good Morning Earth?
- Sure.

1780
01:12:41,132 --> 01:12:44,102
(Exclaiming)

1781
01:12:44,332 --> 01:12:46,632
(They chose the vegetarian combo.)

1782
01:12:46,632 --> 01:12:48,372
Hey. This soup looks good.

1783
01:12:49,672 --> 01:12:50,772
It's not bad.

1784
01:12:50,772 --> 01:12:52,042
(Trying the tomato soup)

1785
01:12:52,342 --> 01:12:53,712
- It's sour.
- Yes.

1786
01:12:54,112 --> 01:12:55,242
I like it.

1787
01:12:55,742 --> 01:12:57,142
You like everything.

1788
01:12:57,612 --> 01:12:58,652
That's not true.

1789
01:13:00,052 --> 01:13:02,122
- Do you want to try dipping it?
- Go ahead.

1790
01:13:04,352 --> 01:13:05,552
Isn't that what it's for?

1791
01:13:09,762 --> 01:13:11,092
(Exclaiming)

1792
01:13:11,392 --> 01:13:13,062
It's not bad when you dip it in the soup.

1793
01:13:14,462 --> 01:13:15,902
In the US culture,

1794
01:13:15,902 --> 01:13:17,972
it's normal to dip the grilled cheese sandwich...

1795
01:13:17,972 --> 01:13:19,632
in the tomato soup.

1796
01:13:20,302 --> 01:13:22,602
Or they dip the crispy toast in the soup.

1797
01:13:25,812 --> 01:13:28,482
(Stir-fry onions, carrots, and celeries.)

1798
01:13:28,482 --> 01:13:31,082
(Then mix them with tomatoes.)

1799
01:13:31,212 --> 01:13:32,852
Next, grind everything.

1800
01:13:35,752 --> 01:13:37,722
Use the fresh cream and butter...

1801
01:13:37,722 --> 01:13:38,952
to make it thick.

1802
01:13:39,222 --> 01:13:41,662
(Tasty and sour tomato soup is ready.)

1803
01:13:45,962 --> 01:13:47,162
It's ready.

1804
01:13:47,492 --> 01:13:49,332
Have a nice trip. Thank you.

1805
01:13:49,862 --> 01:13:54,002
(30 minutes since business began)

1806
01:13:54,102 --> 01:13:55,642
The current sales.

1807
01:13:56,372 --> 01:13:57,442
